1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,611
This tutorial shows how Miftah's chart of
accounts is organised,

2
00:00:03,611 --> 00:00:07,222
how every property gets its own set of
accounts, and

3
00:00:07,222 --> 00:00:10,471
which account each charge on a contract
posts to.

4
00:00:10,471 --> 00:00:14,082
As the Accountant, open Accounting and
choose Chart of Accounts.

5
00:00:14,082 --> 00:00:16,610
The tree groups every account under five

6
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:19,137
types: assets, liabilities, income,
expenses and equity.

7
00:00:19,137 --> 00:00:23,109
Groups such as Rental Receivable and Bank
only hold other accounts.

8
00:00:23,109 --> 00:00:26,359
The accounts beneath them, the leaves, are
where journals

9
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:29,247
post, and a balance is always the sum

10
00:00:29,247 --> 00:00:32,136
of its journal lines, never a typed
figure.

11
00:00:32,136 --> 00:00:35,025
Filter by property and choose Palm Ridge
Residences.

12
00:00:35,025 --> 00:00:37,913
Now you see that building's own accounts:
its

13
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:40,802
Rent Receivable, PDC Receivable, Emirates
Islamic bank account,

14
00:00:40,802 --> 00:00:43,329
Advance Rent, Security Deposit and Rental
Income.

15
00:00:43,329 --> 00:00:46,579
Each building keeps its own books inside
the organisation.

16
00:00:46,579 --> 00:00:50,912
Open the property itself, Palm Ridge
Residences, and its Ledger accounts tab.

17
00:00:50,912 --> 00:00:54,162
Every role, such as Rent Receivable or
Advance Rent,

18
00:00:54,162 --> 00:00:57,050
points to one account for this property,
and

19
00:00:57,050 --> 00:00:59,939
Change maps a role to a different one.

20
00:00:59,939 --> 00:01:03,550
Posting rules only name roles; the
property decides the account.

21
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:06,438
Next, open Property account template under
One-time setup.

22
00:01:06,438 --> 00:01:09,688
For every role there is a name pattern,
where

23
00:01:09,688 --> 00:01:12,938
the placeholder is replaced by the
property's name, and

24
00:01:12,938 --> 00:01:15,826
the parent group the new account files
under.

25
00:01:15,826 --> 00:01:18,354
When a building is added, its account

26
00:01:18,354 --> 00:01:20,881
set is created from this template
automatically.

27
00:01:20,881 --> 00:01:25,214
Further down, Default accounts are the
company-wide accounts that are not per

28
00:01:25,214 --> 00:01:29,186
building: the Cash Account, Output VAT on
Sales, Input VAT on

29
00:01:29,186 --> 00:01:33,158
Purchases, PDC Payable for issued cheques,
and bank charges and interest.

30
00:01:33,158 --> 00:01:34,602
Finally, open Charge types.

31
00:01:34,602 --> 00:01:37,491
These are the charges a contract can
carry.

32
00:01:37,491 --> 00:01:41,102
Rent is earned day by day over the term,
and

33
00:01:41,102 --> 00:01:44,713
a security deposit is held for the tenant,
never income.

34
00:01:44,713 --> 00:01:49,046
For each fee you choose how it is earned:
the Parking Fee

35
00:01:49,046 --> 00:01:53,017
over the term, like rent; the Admin Fee
and the Renewal

36
00:01:53,017 --> 00:01:56,989
Fee once, when charged; and Utilities
recovered at cost, not income.

37
00:01:56,989 --> 00:02:00,600
The charge type decides where each
contract line is credited.
